  "problem": "${7}^{6}\\cdot {(2\\cdot 7)}^{3}=$",
  "worked_solution": "First, we rewrite the second factor using the power of product rule:\n\n$$\n{7}^{6}\\cdot {(2\\cdot 7)}^{3}={7}^{6}\\cdot {2}^{3}\\cdot {7}^{3}\n$$\n\nFinally, we apply the product rule for exponents, and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{7}^{6}\\cdot {2}^{3}\\cdot {7}^{3} & ={7}^{6}\\cdot {7}^{3}\\cdot {2}^{3} \\\\  & ={7}^{6+3}\\cdot {2}^{3} \\\\  & ={7}^{9}\\cdot {2}^{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
